    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Rare (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p>This idol depicts an elephant sitting on its haunches, smiling regally behind its raised trunk.</p><p><strong>Blemished (Uncommon).</strong> The idol is made of tarnished bronze, its surface marked with small dings and dents.</p><p>You can cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplAugury0000]{Augury} from the idol, which speaks the omen aloud in answer. Once the idol has been used to cast this spell, it can’t be used to cast it again until the next dawn.</p><p><strong>Tarnished (Rare).</strong> The idol is made of gold, with a patina of dust settled in its crevices.</p><p>While attuned to the idol, you have a +1 bonus to Armor Class. In addition, while holding the idol, you can take a Magic action to touch a nonmagical trade bar or gemstone and turn it into coins of the same value—touching a 5-pound silver bar, for example, turns it into 25 GP in coins.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-7OKJ3hDls9V5sxaO\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Cette idole évolue : chaque version garde les propriétés des précédentes. Quand elle évolue, remplacez-la par la version suivante (Blemished, Tarnished, puis Golden).</p></section>",
